{
  "schema_version": "3.0",
  "key": "indirect_speech",
  "concept_slug": "indirect_speech",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "Reporting What Someone Said",
  "cefr_level": "B1",
  "goal": "Report statements and questions with at, om, and Norwegian subordinate-clause word order.",
  "elements": [
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "orient",
      "title": "What Indirect Speech Does",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Indirect speech means reporting what someone said instead of quoting their exact words. In Norwegian, reported statements usually use a reporting verb plus "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "at",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", much like English uses that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "For reported statements, use a reporting verb such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "sa",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "fortalte",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "mente",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " followed by "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "at",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " and a clause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun sa at hun var syk."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She said that she was ill."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Læreren fortalte at testen begynte klokka ni."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The teacher told us that the test started at nine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Omar mente at planen var god."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Omar thought that the plan was good."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Reported Statements",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The clause after "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "at",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " is a subordinate clause: a clause inside another sentence. In these clauses, the subject comes before the finite verb. If there is a sentence adverb, an adverb such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ikke",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " that comments on the whole clause, it normally comes before the finite verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "In reported clauses: subject before finite verb, and sentence adverb before the finite verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Han sa at han ikke kom."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "He said that he was not coming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "De fortalte at de aldri hadde vært i Bergen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "They said that they had never been to Bergen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "note",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Norwegian does not require an English-style tense backshift. Choose the tense that fits the meaning. If the statement is still true, Norwegian often keeps the original tense."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "example",
              "no": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Hun sa at hun bor i Oslo."
                }
              ],
              "en": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "She said that she lives in Oslo."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "contrast",
      "title": "Reported Questions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When you report a question, the reported part also behaves like a subordinate clause. For a yes/no question, use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". For a wh-question, keep the question word, such as "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvor",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "når",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", but use normal subordinate-clause word order."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Report yes/no questions with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "spurte om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". Report wh-questions with the question word, and do not use question inversion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun spurte om jeg kunne hjelpe henne."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She asked whether I could help her."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "De spurte om vi ikke hadde tid."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "They asked whether we did not have time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Han spurte hvor jeg bodde."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "He asked where I lived."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Sjefen spurte når møtet begynte."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The manager asked when the meeting started."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Pronouns, Time, and Place",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When you report speech, adjust words that depend on who is speaking, when they are speaking, or where they are. These are deictic words: words whose reference changes with the situation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "col_langs": [
            "en",
            "no",
            "no"
          ],
          "headers": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Shift"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Direkte tale"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Indirekte tale"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "speaker changes"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Jeg er trøtt."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Hun sa at hun var trøtt."
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "listener changes"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Kan du hjelpe meg?"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Han spurte om jeg kunne hjelpe ham."
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "time changes"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Jeg kommer i morgen."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Hun sa at hun kom dagen etter."
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "place changes"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Vi møtes her."
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "De sa at de skulle møtes der."
                }
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "tip",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Do not shift words mechanically. Ask who is reporting, where they are, and when the report happens."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "recap",
      "title": "Core Pattern",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The main move is simple: choose the right reporting verb, choose "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "at",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for statements or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "om",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for yes/no questions, then use subordinate-clause word order."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "Hun sa at hun var klar.",
                "lang": "no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "Han mente at vi ikke trengte mer tid.",
                "lang": "no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "De spurte om bussen kom snart.",
                "lang": "no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "Hun spurte hvor vi bodde.",
                "lang": "no"
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
